@Kolaposki  The rate primarily depends on your service quota, which determines how many tokens per minute you're allowed. You can review your service quotas and adjust the settings accordingly. Typically, accounts have a default limit, which can be quite small—around 4,000 tokens/min, for instance. While that amount is relatively low, quotas vary between accounts. For example, in one of my AWS accounts, the limit is set to 4000, whereas my primary account has a significantly higher quota. You can request an increase by submitting a support ticket for a general issue even though the quota says not adjustable.

Also, for the CNN task, using Haiku with `use_vision = False`, does the job. The CNN task, at most requires around 20k tokens with vision. I usually implement exponential backoff with bedrock when I call it through litellm to avoid throttling issues.
